"""Concrete retellings from the borrower and the manuscript's owner."""

def apply_bag_edits(edits):
    edits[7]['-r'].update({
        0: ('周五晚上我借了陈宇的蓝袋子，带几本书回家。周六上午到了换书活动，我先把书拿出来，再把空袋子放在一楼门右边，准备等他来搬东西时交还。门的两侧都堆着箱子，我把袋子往里挪了一点，免得挡住入口。我想发个消息，手里又有人递来一本书，问放哪儿。我转头帮他找桌子，就把消息忘了。等陈宇来了，我也没有再过去指给他看。', "I borrowed Chen Yu's blue bag on Friday to take some books home. At Saturday's book exchange I removed the books and put the empty bag to the right of the downstairs entrance, ready to return it when he arrived. Boxes lined both sides, so I moved it further in to keep the doorway clear. I meant to message him, but someone handed me a book and asked where it went. Helping them find a table, I forgot the message. When Chen Yu arrived, I didn't go back to show him either."),
        3: ('陈宇把第四页拿起来，指着最后一行给我看，说这一句昨晚才改。我问是不是他搬桌子时掉的，他摇头，说搬的是桌子，稿子早就放进袋里了。我让他先拿好这张，自己回门口问负责收东西的人。刚走到门边，就听见志愿者说蓝袋子也搬上去了。陈宇跟在后面，一听二楼两个字就跑了过来，问仓库的门现在开着没有。', "Chen Yu picked up page four and pointed to its last line, which he'd revised the night before. Had he dropped it while moving tables? No: he'd been carrying a table, with the pages already in the bag. I asked him to keep the sheet while I went back to the entrance. A volunteer said the blue bag had gone upstairs too. Hearing 'second floor,' Chen Yu hurried over to ask whether the storeroom was open."),
        4: ('负责门口的志愿者说，他把蓝袋子和两只纸箱一起搬到二楼仓库了。门口越来越满，有人推着椅子过不去，他就先把这些东西移开，以为袋子也是活动待用的。他还记得上楼时有纸露在袋口。我问里面是不是放书，他说没打开看，放到纸箱旁就下来了。陈宇举起手里的第四页，问能不能带我们上去，志愿者马上放下正在整理的书，领我们往楼梯走。', "The entrance volunteer had moved the blue bag and two boxes to the upstairs storeroom. Someone pushing chairs couldn't get through the crowded doorway, so he'd cleared what he assumed was event equipment. He remembered paper sticking out of the bag. Had it contained books? He hadn't opened it; he'd set it beside the boxes and come back down. Chen Yu held up page four and asked to be taken upstairs. The volunteer put down the books he was sorting and led us to the stairs."),
        5: ('我们沿着楼道上去，仓库里正有人收椅子。管理员把门开大一点，让我们从旁边进去。蓝袋子就在靠墙的纸箱旁，陈宇拿起来，先把稿子放到空桌上。里面还有四张，他一张一张排开，一、二、三、五都在。我把楼道那张递过去，他放进三和五中间，又从第一句读到新改的那一句。听见第四页接上了，我才敢把手里的袋子放下，问他这回能排练了吧。', "Upstairs, someone was putting chairs away. The manager opened the door wider to let us through. Chen Yu found the blue bag beside the boxes and laid its four remaining sheets on an empty table: one, two, three and five. I handed over the corridor sheet; he put it between three and five and read through to his new line. Only when page four fitted did I put down the bag and ask whether we could finally rehearse."),
        6: ('志愿者说抱歉，刚才应该先问一句。陈宇说找到了就好，下次自己把袋口拉好。我也拿出手机，把蓝袋子已找到发到群里，免得大家还往别处跑。门口仍然有人搬书，志愿者指着另一张桌子，问个人东西放那边行不行。我说行，帮他把桌上的活动资料移开，再贴上一张写着个人物品的纸。陈宇拿着稿子过来，笑说现在先别把这五张也当成交换的书。', "The volunteer apologised for not asking before moving it. Chen Yu was glad we'd found it and would close the bag properly next time. I messaged the group so nobody kept searching elsewhere. With books still passing through the entrance, the volunteer suggested another table for personal belongings. I helped clear the event handouts and label it. Arriving with the manuscript, Chen Yu joked that these five sheets weren't exchange books either."),
        8: ('排练开始时，陈宇从第一句读起，读到第四页还把纸举起来给大家看了一下，大家都笑了。那张纸有一道新折痕，但字还能看清。他把纸按在桌上，说这里先别翻，让我把这句读完。我接着读自己的下一句，才发现刚才顾着找袋子，把开头的词忘了。陈宇说这回纸没丢，倒是台词丢了。我让他从前一句再来，两个人又试了一遍，这次总算接上。', "Chen Yu began at the first line and held page four up for everyone to see when he reached it, making everyone laugh. Its new crease didn't obscure the words. Holding it against the table, he asked me not to turn it until he'd finished the line. I tried my next line and realised I'd forgotten its opening while searching for the bag. The paper was safe this time, he joked, but we'd lost the dialogue. I asked him to repeat the previous line; on the second attempt we finally joined it up."),
        9: ('晚上一个没来活动的朋友发消息，问怎么群里找了一上午袋子。我回他说周五我借回家，周六把空袋子还到门边；陈宇后来放进去五页稿子，去搬桌子时，志愿者又把袋子和纸箱搬上二楼。我们在楼道找到第四页，在仓库找到其余四页，已经排完了。他问纸还能不能用，我拍了一张照片发过去，折痕还在，字也看得清。陈宇在旁边补了一句，下次直接带副本，原稿留家里。', "That evening an absent friend asked why the group had spent the morning looking for a bag. I messaged back: I'd borrowed it Friday and returned it empty Saturday; Chen Yu had added five script pages, then gone to move tables while a volunteer took the bag and boxes upstairs. We found page four in the corridor and the other four in the storeroom, and had finished rehearsing. Were the pages usable? I sent a photo showing the crease and legible words. Chen Yu added that he'd bring copies next time and leave the originals at home."),
    })
    edits[7]['-paired-reading'].update({
        1: ('林安说早上把空袋子放到门右边。我听见空就急了，问怎么会空，我明明放进去五张。她让我先听完，说空是早上还的时候，那时我还没到。我这才想起自己来了以后打开过袋子，里面确实没有书，正好放稿子。她问放完以后呢，我说去搬桌子了。桌子太重，刚才两个人抬了半天，等我再回来，原来的位置只剩两只空箱子。', "Lin An said she'd left the empty bag to the right of the entrance. Empty? I'd put five pages in it! Let her finish, she said: it had been empty when she returned it, before I'd arrived. Then I remembered opening it myself and finding no books, leaving room for my manuscript. What had I done afterwards? Moved tables. The table was heavy and had taken two of us a while; by the time I returned, only two empty boxes remained at the spot."),
        2: ('有人说东西都搬到地下室了，我已经转身往楼梯走。林安叫住我，让我先问有没有见到蓝袋子。那个人想了一下，说只是记得上次活动放在那里，今天没有看见。我只好折回来，去问门口的志愿者。他正忙着搬书，让我等一下。我站到旁边，往楼道里看，一张纸躺在地上。林安走过去捡起来，我一看页码，正好是刚才还在找的第四页。', "Someone said things had gone to the basement, and I was already heading for the stairs when Lin An called me back to ask whether they'd seen the bag. No; they only remembered the previous event. I returned to the entrance volunteer, who was busy moving books and asked me to wait. Looking down the corridor, I spotted a sheet on the floor. Lin An picked it up. Its number was four—the page I'd been looking for."),
        3: ('我拿着第四页，说稿子不是一直在袋里吗。林安问后来也看着吗，我摇头，改口说放进去时还在，后来我去搬桌子了。她指着门边，让我想想袋口有没有拉好。我记得拿纸时两只手都忙，就那么放了进去，接着有人叫我搬桌子。看着手里折过的纸，我越来越想快点找到另外四张。志愿者这时走过来，问是不是在找那个蓝袋子，我赶紧说对。', "Holding page four, I asked whether the pages hadn't been in the bag the whole time. Had I watched afterwards? No—I corrected myself: they'd been there when I put them in, then I'd moved tables. Lin An asked if I'd closed the bag. Both hands had been busy with the sheets, and someone had called me away. Looking at the folded paper, I wanted to find the other four quickly. Then the volunteer came over: were we looking for the blue bag? Yes, I said at once."),
        6: ('我们跟志愿者一起把个人东西挪到另一张桌子，林安贴了说明。我把蓝袋子提起来给他看，问下次能不能先留在这边。他说可以，不过结束以后记得拿走，晚上还要收桌子。林安笑着说这回看见了，已经不在门边了。我让她先拿袋子，自己把稿子收成一叠。管理员在旁边叫我们再腾出一点地方，刚收好的椅子还要搬过来，我们又往里站了一点。', "We moved the personal belongings to another table and Lin An labelled it. I asked the volunteer if the blue bag could stay there next time. Yes, but take it home afterwards; the tables would be cleared at night. Lin An laughed: she'd seen this move, and it was no longer by the door. She held the bag while I gathered the manuscript into a stack. The manager needed room for the chairs he'd just put away, so we moved further inside."),
        7: ('排练前林安说这次袋子我拿，桌子你搬，大家都笑了。我说好，不过伞还是你自己拿。她看了一眼靠门的伞，说伞没动过，你先把桌子搬好。我把桌子推到灯旁，稿子放在上面，等大家坐下才拿起来读。排练结束以后，我把五页都收进自己的背包，林安把空蓝袋子还给我。我拉上两只包的口，她在旁边看着，笑说现在终于能走了吧。', "Before rehearsal Lin An said she'd hold the bag and I'd move the table. Everyone laughed. Fine, but she was carrying her own umbrella. It hadn't moved, she said; get the table into place first. I pushed it beside the lamp, put the manuscript on it and picked it up to read once everyone sat down. Afterwards I put all five pages in my backpack, and Lin An handed me the empty blue bag. As I closed both bags, she laughed: could we finally leave?"),
        8: ('晚饭时有人问，是不是有人拿走了我们的资料。我说是志愿者把袋子和箱子搬到楼上，不是带出楼房。他问怎么还有一张在楼道，我把第四页拿给他看，说可能上楼时从没拉好的袋口掉出来了，具体哪一下没看见。林安在旁边补充，她捡到时就在楼道地上。朋友摸了摸那道折痕，说还好没踩上。我说字都能看清，刚才已经拿它排完了，今晚回家再压一压。', "At dinner someone asked if our materials had been taken away. The volunteer had moved the bag and boxes upstairs, I said, not out of the building. What about the sheet in the corridor? I showed page four; it might have fallen from the unclosed bag on the way up, though I hadn't seen the moment. Lin An said she'd found it on the corridor floor. Our friend touched the crease: lucky nobody stepped on it. The words were clear and we'd rehearsed with it; I'd press it flat at home."),
        9: ('回家后我把第四页夹进一本厚书，其他四张放在桌上，准备明天一起交给演出的人。林安发消息问还心疼吗，我说一点点，毕竟是自己改了好多遍的原稿。她说下次带副本吧，我拿出手机把五页都拍下来，第二天打印一份，改把副本交给演出的人。原来的收在家里，活动带新印的。蓝袋子倒还可以借，她一问我就说行，不过这次还回来记得告诉我放哪儿，别让我再问一上午。', "At home I pressed page four inside a thick book, leaving the other sheets on the desk to hand to the performers tomorrow. Lin An asked if I was still upset. A little: I'd revised that original so many times. Bring copies next time, she said. I photographed all five and printed a set the next day to give the performers instead. I'd keep the originals at home and take the fresh copies to events. She could still borrow the blue bag—just tell me where she'd returned it, so I didn't spend another morning asking."),
    })
